    <!-- Slide 7 -->
    <div class="slide">
        <div class="slide-header">
            <div class="slide-title">The Defendant: XYZ Corporation</div>
            <div class="slide-number">Slide 07</div>
        </div>
        <div class="slide-body">
            <div class="content-block">
                <h3>Company Overview</h3>
                <p><strong>XYZ Corporation</strong> is a national manufacturer of industrial building materials, specializing in commercial loading dock solutions.</p>
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    <h4 style="color: var(--primary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Role in Incident</h4>
                    <p>XYZ Corporation designed, manufactured, and distributed the Model 500 Heavy Metal Roll-Up Door installed at Mr. Doe's place of employment.</p>
                </div>
                <ul style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
                    <li>Responsible for product design and safety engineering</li>
                    <li>Manufactured the tension spring mechanism at fault</li>
                    <li>Distributed product without adequate safety warnings</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="footer-bar"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- Slide 8 -->
    <div class="slide">
        <div class="slide-header">
            <div class="slide-title">The Defect</div>
            <div class="slide-number">Slide 08</div>
        </div>
        <div class="slide-body">
            <div class="content-block">
                <h3>Design Defect: Tension Spring Failure</h3>
                <p>The Model 500 door contained a critical design flaw in its counter-balancing tension spring system.</p>
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    <p><strong>Failure Mode:</strong> Inadequate spring retention clips allowed the main tension spring to disengage under load stress, causing the 300lb door to free-fall without resistance.</p>
                </div>
                <ul style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    <li>Lack of redundant safety mechanisms (no secondary brake)</li>
                    <li>Failure to include auto-reverse sensor technology</li>
                    <li>Direct causal link between defect and plaintiff's head injury</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="footer-bar"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- Slide 9 -->
    <div class="slide">
        <div class="slide-header">
            <div class="slide-title">Legal Basis</div>
            <div class="slide-number">Slide 09</div>
        </div>
        <div class="slide-body">
            <div class="content-block">
                <h3>California Product Liability Law</h3>
                <p>Plaintiff brings claims under California's strict product liability doctrine, holding manufacturers accountable for defective products that enter the stream of commerce.</p>
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    <h4 style="color: var(--primary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Violated Regulations</h4>
                    <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                        <li>Cal-OSHA Safety Orders regarding industrial door mechanisms</li>
                        <li>ANSI Z97.1 Standard for safety glazing and door performance</li>
                        <li>California Civil Code §1714 (Negligence)</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="footer-bar"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- Slide 10 -->
    <div class="slide">
        <div class="slide-header">
            <div class="slide-title">Testing Process</div>
            <div class="slide-number">Slide 10</div>
        </div>
        <div class="slide-body">
            <div class="content-grid">
                <div class="content-block">
                    <h3>XYZ Corporation Internal Testing</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Limited to 500 cycle testing (industry standard is 10,000+)</li>
                        <li>Failed to test for sudden spring disengagement</li>
                        <li>No real-world load stress testing performed</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="content-block">
                    <h3>Third-Party Independent Testing</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Commissioned by plaintiff's legal team</li>
                        <li>Tested by National Safety Laboratories (NSL)</li>
                        <li>Replicated the failure in 3 of 5 test cycles</li>
                        <li>Confirmed absence of secondary safety mechanisms</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="footer-bar"></div>
    </div>

